  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Find all rational roots of the following polynomials:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^4+3x^3+4x^2+3x+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$.",
          "worked": "By the Integer Root Theorem, the only possible rational roots are $\\pm1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+3+4+3+1\\\\P(1)&=12\\ne0\\\\P(-1)&=1-3+4-3+1\\\\P(-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe only rational root is $x=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^3-x^2-3x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "By the Rational Root Theorem, the only possible rational roots are $\\pm1,\\ \\pm\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=2-1-3-1=-3\\ne0\\\\P(-1)&=-2-1+3-1=-1\\ne0\\\\P\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=\\frac14-\\frac14-\\frac32-1=-\\frac52\\ne0\\\\P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)&=-\\frac14-\\frac14+\\frac32-1=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe only rational root is $x=-\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^4+3x^3+6x^2+7x+3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$.",
          "worked": "By the Integer Root Theorem, the only possible rational roots are $\\pm1,\\ \\pm3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+3+6+7+3=20\\ne0\\\\P(-1)&=1-3+6-7+3=0\\\\P(3)&=81+81+54+21+3=240\\ne0\\\\P(-3)&=81-81+54-21+3=36\\ne0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe only rational root is $x=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^5-4x^4+2x^3+2x^2+x+6=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.\n\nTest the integer divisors of $6$.",
          "worked": "By the Integer Root Theorem, the only possible rational roots are $\\pm1,\\ \\pm2,\\ \\pm3,\\ \\pm6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-4+2+2+1+6=8\\ne0\\\\P(-1)&=-1-4-2+2-1+6=0\\\\P(2)&=32-64+16+8+2+6=0\\\\P(-2)&=-32-64-16+8-2+6=-100\\ne0\\\\P(3)&=243-324+54+18+3+6=0\\\\P(-3)&=-243-324-54+18-3+6=-600\\ne0\\\\P(6)&=7776-5184+432+72+6+6=3108\\ne0\\\\P(-6)&=-7776-5184-432+72-6+6=-13320\\ne0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe rational roots are $x=-1,\\ 2,\\ 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^4+x^3-19x^2-9x+9=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac12,\\ 3,\\ -3,\\ -1$.\n\nTest the Rational Root Theorem candidates.",
          "worked": "By the Rational Root Theorem, the only possible rational roots are $\\pm1,\\ \\pm3,\\ \\pm9,\\ \\pm\\frac12,\\ \\pm\\frac32,\\ \\pm\\frac92$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=-16\\ne0\\\\P(-1)&=0\\\\P(3)&=0\\\\P(-3)&=0\\\\P(9)&=12240\\ne0\\\\P(-9)&=10944\\ne0\\\\P\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=\\frac18+\\frac18-\\frac{19}{4}-\\frac92+9=0\\\\P\\left(-\\frac12\\right)&=\\frac{35}{4}\\ne0\\\\P\\left(\\frac32\\right)&=-\\frac{135}{4}\\ne0\\\\P\\left(-\\frac32\\right)&=-\\frac{27}{2}\\ne0\\\\P\\left(\\frac92\\right)&=495\\ne0\\\\P\\left(-\\frac92\\right)&=\\frac{1575}{4}\\ne0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe rational roots are $x=\\frac12,\\ 3,\\ -3,\\ -1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      }
    ]
  },
